# What must not enter the CI image.
#
# The first entry is the important one. Without it the build context carries the whole history, the
# image gets a .git directory, and any check could quietly start asking git questions instead of
# examining the tree it was given. The commit identity is supposed to arrive as CI_COMMIT, resolved
# on the host and re-verified after the run — see scripts/submit-pr.mjs. Leaving .git out is what
# keeps that the only route.
.git

# .gitignore is deliberately NOT excluded. It was, briefly, on the reflex that anything starting
# with ".git" is history — and the pipeline went red, because a check reads it. It is tree content,
# committed and reviewed like any other file, and a check is entitled to ask what it says.

# Evidence from previous runs. Copying it in would mean a stale receipt could survive into a fresh
# image and be mistaken for this run's result.
artifacts/local-ci

# Developer-machine state. None of this exists in this repository today; the entries are here so
# that the day one of them appears, it does not silently join the build context.
node_modules
.env
.env.*
*.log
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
